Text post (code in backticks): '```ts
let x = 5;
x = "5";
```
What does TypeScript report for line 2?'  A) Type error, x was inferred as number  B) x changes to string  C) x becomes number | string  D) x is any. Ask for the letter and one sentence why. Do not reveal the answer in the post. At 18:00 reply to own post with the answer (A) and the bank explanation: 'Inference from the initializer fixes the type at number.' Source: devShark question bank (lib/roadmap-questions-*.ts), tag TypeScript. Link only in that answer reply: devshark.app/daily?utm_source=threads&utm_medium=reply&utm_campaign=qotd (/daily from #239; fall back to /quiz if not shipped). Draft comes from marketingShark's quiz package Threads caption (Queue 07:00); owner approves and posts manually until quorum#587 lands.

Text post (code in backticks): '```ts
let value: any = 5;
value = "now a string";
```
What does the checker report?'  A) Type error  B) No error: any accepts any type  C) Runtime error  D) A warning to use unknown. Ask for the letter and one sentence why. Do not reveal the answer in the post. At 18:00 reply to own post with the answer (B) and the bank explanation: '`any` opts out of checking, which is why `unknown` is the safer default.' Source: devShark question bank (lib/roadmap-questions-*.ts), tag TypeScript. Link only in that answer reply: devshark.app/daily?utm_source=threads&utm_medium=reply&utm_campaign=qotd (/daily from #239; fall back to /quiz if not shipped). Draft comes from marketingShark's quiz package Threads caption (Queue 07:00); owner approves and posts manually until quorum#587 lands.

Text post (code in backticks): '```ts
const firstName: string = "Ada";
firstName.length;
```
What type is `firstName.length`?'  A) string  B) number  C) any  D) 3. Ask for the letter and one sentence why. Do not reveal the answer in the post. At 18:00 reply to own post with the answer (B) and the bank explanation: '`length` is a number; the literal 3 is its value, not its type.' Source: devShark question bank (lib/roadmap-questions-*.ts), tag TypeScript. Link only in that answer reply: devshark.app/daily?utm_source=threads&utm_medium=reply&utm_campaign=qotd (/daily from #239; fall back to /quiz if not shipped). Owner picks it from the prepared QOTD sheet (prelaunch ds-pre-15).
